## 4. Proposition A4.2(2): population maj3 after the first event (d = 4 cube)
 residual after the 9-gate refit equals -x1x2x3/2: True
 max |U| over depth-one candidates: 1.11e-16
 max over source pairs of |hat(ab)(123)| = 0.5000 (lemma: <= 1/2)
   |U| = 0.2500: 12 distinct functions (up to sign): XOR(x1,AND(x2,x3)), XOR(x1,AND(~x2,~x3)), XOR(x2,AND(x1,x3)), XOR(x2,AND(~x1,~x3)), XOR(x3,AND(x1,x2)), XOR(x3,AND(~x1,~x2)), XOR(AND(x1,x2),AND(x1,x3)), XOR(AND(x1,x2),AND(x2,x3)), XOR(AND(~x1,~x2),AND(~x1,~x3)), XOR(AND(~x1,~x2),AND(~x2,~x3)), XOR(AND(x1,x3),AND(x2,x3)), XOR(AND(~x1,~x3),AND(~x2,~x3))
   |U| = 0.1250: 20 distinct functions (up to sign)
   |U| = 0.0000: 55 distinct functions (up to sign)
 each maximizer alone completes the representation of maj3: True
 distinct gate functions after the second event: 9 + 12 = 21; residual after refit on all: 4.4e-16
 second event time: 2 Theta + Theta/0.25 = 6.00 Theta; other clocks at that time <= 0.50 Theta

